{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01008",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.67,
      "end_seconds": 4.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Hello, sorry about the delay, do sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.16,
      "end_seconds": 7.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Evening, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 8.12,
      "end_seconds": 12.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.63,
      "end_seconds": 25.26,
      "duration_seconds": 8.63,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together. Right, did the receptionist sort you out quickly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.89,
      "end_seconds": 29.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Yes, she was lovely about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.32,
      "end_seconds": 33.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.25,
      "end_seconds": 47.2,
      "duration_seconds": 12.95,
      "text": "Well, I've been having sharp pain in the upper right of my tummy. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.28,
      "end_seconds": 54.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.03,
      "end_seconds": 70.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.06,
      "end_seconds": 97.56,
      "duration_seconds": 9.5,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 121 over 73, pulse is 83 beats a minute, SpO2 97 percent on room air. And temp 36.4 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.66,
      "end_seconds": 103.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.58,
      "end_seconds": 112.03,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "We'll look at it together shortly. So, can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.75,
      "end_seconds": 114.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Probably two weeks. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.07,
      "end_seconds": 126.05,
      "duration_seconds": 9.98,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.79,
      "end_seconds": 134.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "Mm, it happens all the time. Only lying still, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.75,
      "end_seconds": 139.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "So, any nausea after meals as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.05,
      "end_seconds": 144.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.0,
      "end_seconds": 148.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.08,
      "end_seconds": 155.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Mild, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.74,
      "end_seconds": 165.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Okay, a few quick ones: dark urine or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.69,
      "end_seconds": 171.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "I haven't had dark urine or weight loss, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.17,
      "end_seconds": 176.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "A few quick ones: black stools, pale stools or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.9,
      "end_seconds": 183.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "I haven't had black stools, pale stools or fever, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.32,
      "end_seconds": 186.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.86,
      "end_seconds": 189.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.22,
      "end_seconds": 200.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.6,
      "end_seconds": 203.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.02,
      "end_seconds": 219.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "So, are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.77,
      "end_seconds": 228.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "Not currently, but as a youngster diclofenac gave me swelling of my lips."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.68,
      "end_seconds": 247.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.54,
      "end_seconds": 259.93,
      "duration_seconds": 11.39,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day. My partner and our baby. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.71,
      "end_seconds": 262.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 263.89,
      "end_seconds": 267.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "It's atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.76,
      "end_seconds": 273.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.02,
      "end_seconds": 276.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "I've got high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.8,
      "end_seconds": 281.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "I follow. Alright, high cholesterol, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.78,
      "end_seconds": 289.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.31,
      "end_seconds": 292.01,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.82,
      "end_seconds": 294.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.39,
      "end_seconds": 309.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.92,
      "text": "There is tenderness under the right ribs when you breathe in, and no yellowing of the eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.52,
      "end_seconds": 327.61,
      "duration_seconds": 15.09,
      "text": "You can relax now. Okay, thinking it through, it fits best with biliary colic from gallstones. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I'd also keep peptic ulcer in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.21,
      "end_seconds": 332.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Oh, is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.44,
      "end_seconds": 354.73,
      "duration_seconds": 21.29,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now biliary colic from gallstones is my leading thought, not anything worse. Just to be sure I understood. You've had sharp pain in the upper right of your tummy for two weeks, and no black stools or dark urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.42,
      "end_seconds": 357.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.55,
      "end_seconds": 395.65,
      "duration_seconds": 28.1,
      "text": "I'm going to order liver blood tests, for upper abdominal pain. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'm going to order an ultrasound of the tummy, for right upper quadrant pain. Keep meals small and low in fat until we have the scan. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 396.0,
      "end_seconds": 406.3,
      "duration_seconds": 10.3,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. Please don't wait if you develop a fever, yellow eyes or severe constant pain. That's when to be seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 407.99,
      "end_seconds": 409.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Yes, will do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.91,
      "end_seconds": 413.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "We'll catch up in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 414.16,
      "end_seconds": 417.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "I'll note it in my calendar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 419.43,
      "end_seconds": 423.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.11,
      "end_seconds": 427.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}